    "name": "Gold Beets",
    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Golden beets are&nbsp;vibrant, yellow-orange root vegetables known for their&nbsp;</span><b><strong class=\"lexical-text-editor--bold\" style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">mild, sweet flavor and less earthy taste</strong></b><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">&nbsp;than red beets, featuring bright yellow flesh that doesn't \"bleed\" color when cooked, making them visually appealing in salads, roasted dishes, and pickled. They have smooth, firm skin and offer similar nutrients to red beets, with edible greens that taste like spinach, providing versatility and a pop of color in many recipes.&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p>",
